omb or finish yourself. Same with BlackJoker.\n\nBut note: if you don’t play now, and instead pass, you would stall — but **passing is allowed only if you choose**, and here you *can* play. However, look at the valid moves: passing is an option, but is it legal?\n\nWait: The "Last Play to Beat" is ♥A — which was played by your teammate. Then the landlord passed. Now it\'s your turn. Since the last non-pass play was ♥A (a single), you must either beat it or pass.\n\nYou can beat it with:\n- Any single higher than ♥A: that includes 2s and jokers.\nSo ♦2 and BlackJoker are legal.\n\nBut should you play?\n\nIf you play a high card like ♦2 or BlackJoker now, you waste it when your teammate might be about to win. They have only 2 cards left. If they have the lead next, they could go out. But if you take the lead now, you might then be forced to play again, and the landlord could follow.\n\nBetter: **Let your teammate retain initiative.** But you cannot “give” them the lead unless you pass.\n\nHowever, you cannot legally pass unless you cannot beat the last play. But you *can* beat it — you have higher singles.\n\nWait: Rule clarification — in Dou Dizhu, **you may always choose to pass even if you can play**. Passing is optional regardless of having cards to beat.\n\nTherefore, despite being able to beat ♥A, you are allowed to pass.\n\nGiven that your teammate just played a high card (♥A) and likely wants control, and they have only 2 cards left, the best cooperative move is to **pass** and let the turn go back to the landlord. If the landlord cannot play or plays low, your teammate might get another chance.\n\nBut if you play ♦2 or BlackJoker now, you take control, but then the landlord will likely pass, and your teammate will have to respond to your super-high card — but they probably don’t have anything higher (they just played ♥A), so they’ll pass, and then you’d have to lead again — possibly forcing you to waste more high cards.\n\nThus, better to pass and preserve your high cards for later defense.\n\nBut wait — after a player plays a card, others must respond or pass. Sequence:\n\n- Prev Player (teammate): ♥A\n- Next Player (landlord): Pass\n- Now You: Must either beat ♥A or pass.\n\nYou can pass.\n\nAfter you pass, the trick ends. Then it becomes a new round — and the player who played the last un-beaten card leads next. That would be your teammate — **Left (teammate)** gets to lead the next round!\n\nThat’s ideal: your teammate has 2 cards left — if they get to lead, they can play one or both and possibly win the game.\n\nTherefore, **you must pass** to allow your teammate to regain lead and play next.\n\nReason: By passing, you enable your teammate (who has only 2 cards left) to lead the next round, giving them the opportunity to play and potentially win the game. Playing a high card like ♦2 or BlackJoker now would steal momentum and waste powerful cards unnecessarily.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
